# {{.Name}} — domain context

The ubiquitous language lives HERE. One page: the domain's nouns, spelled the
way the whole product spells them — package names, route paths, scope strings,
table names, TypeScript types and ticket prose all use THESE words. A concept
that needs renaming gets renamed here first, then everywhere, in one landing.

Agents and humans read this before naming anything. Keep it short; a glossary
nobody maintains is worse than none.

## Glossary

| Term | Meaning | Spelled in code as |
|---|---|---|
| _e.g. inspection_ | _one pass of a device over a wire_ | `inspections` (feature), `Inspection` (type), `inspections.read` (scope) |

## Actors

Who calls this product, and with what identity — a human role, a device fleet,
a sibling service. One line each.

## Boundaries

What this product deliberately does NOT own (the system of record elsewhere,
the upstream that publishes what we consume). A sentence per boundary saves a
feature per misunderstanding.
